## 📌 Q1. Pair Sum Using Two Pointers

### 🎯 Problem
Find whether a pair of numbers in a sorted array adds up to the target.

### 💻 Code
```java
int arr[] = {1, 2, 4, 6, 8};
int target = 10;

int left = 0;
int right = arr.length - 1;
boolean found = false;

while (left < right) {
    int sum = arr[left] + arr[right];

    if (sum == target) {
        found = true;
        break;
    } else if (sum < target) {
        left++;
    } else {
        right--;
    }
}

System.out.println(found);
```

### Output
```text
true
```

### Dry Run
- `1 + 8 = 9` → sum is small, move `left`.
- `2 + 8 = 10` → target found.

**Time:** O(n)  
**Extra Space:** O(1)

**Interview Tip:** This two-pointer approach works when the array is sorted.

