## 📌 Q2. Pair Sum with a Different Target

### 🎯 Problem
Find whether two numbers add up to `14`.

### 💻 Code
```java
int arr[] = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11};
int target = 14;

int left = 0;
int right = arr.length - 1;
boolean found = false;

while (left < right) {
    int sum = arr[left] + arr[right];

    if (sum == target) {
        found = true;
        break;
    } else if (sum < target) {
        left++;
    } else {
        right--;
    }
}

System.out.println(found);
```

### Output
```text
true
```

### Dry Run
`2 + 11 = 13` → move left.  
`3 + 11 = 14` → target found.

**Time:** O(n)  
**Extra Space:** O(1)

**Remember:** Small sum → move left forward. Large sum → move right backward.

