## 📌 Q10. First Non-Repeating Element

### 🎯 Problem
Find the first element that appears exactly once.

### 💻 Code
```java
int arr[] = {4, 5, 1, 2, 1, 4, 5};

for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    int count = 0;

    for (int j = 0; j < arr.length; j++) {
        if (arr[i] == arr[j]) {
            count++;
        }
    }

    if (count == 1) {
        System.out.println(
            "First non-repeating element: " + arr[i]
        );
        break;
    }
}
```

### Output
```text
First non-repeating element: 2
```

### Dry Run

| Element | Frequency | Result |
|---:|---:|---|
| 4 | 2 | Repeating |
| 5 | 2 | Repeating |
| 1 | 2 | Repeating |
| 2 | 1 | First non-repeating |

When `count == 1`, print the element and stop with `break`.

**Time:** O(n²)  
**Extra Space:** O(1)

**Common Mistake:** Reset `count = 0` inside the outer loop so each element gets a fresh count.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

